course: dictionary
lesson: 10648
title: One word, many joins
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word union comes from a Latin word meaning one. Its basic meaning is joining things together. You can see this in every meaning of the word, from workers to countries to numbers.
explain: «The workers formed a trade union to protect their pay and rights.» Here a union is a group of people who join together. A trade union is a group of workers, so the context shows it is a group, not a team of sports players.
explain: «Old rivals, such as France and Spain, now work together in the European Union.» The clue is «together»: the European Union is a group of countries joined together. In maths, the union of two sets is also a joining: it puts every member of both sets into one new set, with each one listed once.
fact: Union means the act of joining things together.
fact: A trade union is a group of workers who join together to protect their pay and rights.
fact: A union can also be a group of countries or states joined together, such as the European Union.
fact: In maths, A ∪ B is the union of two sets: every member of both sets, each listed once.
fact: In rugby union, «a try» is worth 5, but union here is the name of the sport, not a group of people or countries.
exercise: «Old rivals, such as France and Spain, now work together in the European Union.» What is the European Union? | *A group of countries joined together | A group of workers who protect their pay | A club for university students | A football match between two teams
exercise: Set A is {1, 2, 3} and set B is {3, 4}. What is the union A ∪ B? | {1, 2, 3, 3, 4} | {1, 2} | *{1, 2, 3, 4} | {3}
exercise: Which word means the act of joining things together? | unicorn | uniform | *union | unit
test: «The workers formed a trade union to protect their pay.» What does union mean here? | A group of countries | A meeting of teachers at school | A type of football team | *A group of workers who join together
test: «After the Second World War the USA and the Soviet Union became rivals.» What is the Soviet Union? | A race between two classmates | *A group of states joined together | A ship that sailed across the sea | A team of workers from one school
exam: In maths, what does the union of two sets A ∪ B mean? | The members of A that are not in B | *Every member of both sets, each listed once | Only the members that are in both sets | The number of members in set A
